  "bead": {
    "id": "pqueue-103570d4",
    "title": "Validate ESF entity schemas before every pqueue write",
    "description": "Compile QueueDefinition.entity_schema once per queue and validate typed item documents pre-commit on every write path. Previous fixes covered most backend paths, but focused review found remaining blockers: SegmentedObjectLogInMemoryBackend lacks a schema cache and accepts invalid entity documents through both push paths; MemoryBackend validates push/push_with_request_id and commit_transition lifecycle_items after cmd_seq/item counter reservation, so rejected writes consume externally visible item-id counter space. Fix these gaps. Rejection must happen before durable append, SQL mutation, projection apply, idempotency recording, command sequence mutation, or item-id counter reservation where validation can be known first. In-scope files: pqueue-memory, pqueue-server object_log_sqlite segmented in-memory backend, and targeted tests. Out-of-scope: secondary index key replacement.",
    "acceptance": "cargo fmt --check passes; cargo test -p pqueue schema_validation -- --nocapture passes; cargo test -p pqueue-conformance storage_conformance -- --nocapture passes; backend-specific tests prove invalid entity push and push_with_request_id reject before durable mutation/idempotency on memory, sqlite log, sqlite relational, objectlog, object_log_sqlite composite paths, SegmentedObjectLogInMemoryBackend, and env-gated postgres paths where available; memory tests prove invalid push, push_with_request_id, and commit_transition lifecycle_items do not consume the next valid item id/counter-visible sequence; sqlite relational vectorized commit with invalid lifecycle_items rejects the entry without creating lifecycle items; rg -n 'build_push_items|record_push_idempotency|commit_command|append|counters.reserve|cmd_seq|validate_entity' crates/pqueue-memory/src crates/pqueue-sqlite/src crates/pqueue-postgres/src crates/pqueue-objectlog/src crates/pqueue-server/src/object_log_sqlite.rs shows validation immediately before push/request-id durable mutation sites and before counter reservation for invalid documents.",
    "parent": "pqueue-fc8ef1aa",
